{"content":[{"id":"7e753593","settings":{"display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"d420fd3"}]},"elements":[{"id":"66eb5057","settings":{"__dynamic__":{"image":"[elementor-tag id=\"\" name=\"post-featured-image\" settings=\"%7B%22fallback%22%3A%7B%22url%22%3A%22%22%2C%22id%22%3A%22%22%2C%22size%22%3A%22%22%7D%7D\"]"},"display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"a45fd20"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"theme-post-featured-image","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"5a201779","settings":{"display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"5a3bc6b"}]},"elements":[{"id":"7112bd11","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It is a typical summer afternoon in Dry Prong. Your AC has been running for hours, trying to keep up with the heat and humidity. Then something feels off. The air is not as cool, the system sounds louder than usual, and your home starts to feel uncomfortable.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For many homeowners, this is the moment they realize something is wrong. The truth is, most air conditioners do not fail suddenly. They show warning signs weeks or even months in advance. The problem is that these signs are easy to overlook until the system is pushed to its limit.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Understanding the early signs your AC is dying can help you act before your system breaks down when you need it most.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"210a5cea","settings":{"title":"Key Takeaways\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"647db692","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you are noticing signs your AC is dying, such as air conditioner blowing warm air, frequent short cycling, or weak airflow, your system may not survive peak summer demand. In Dry Prong, LA, where heat and humidity put extra strain on cooling systems, small issues can quickly turn into a full cooling system breakdown. Addressing these warning signs early through HVAC maintenance or professional inspection can help you avoid emergency repairs and costly replacements.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1f679e61","settings":{"title":"Why AC Problems Show Up During the First Real Heatwave\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"42a6448f","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Air conditioners are often under their greatest stress during the hottest stretch of the year. In Central Louisiana, systems can run for long hours without much downtime, especially when humidity levels stay high.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This creates several challenges:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ashrae.org\/technical-resources\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Increased system pressure<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> due to higher cooling demand<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Longer run cycles that expose weak components<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Greater strain on electrical parts, increasing risk of capacitor failure<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6caba6fc","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Many systems that seem fine in spring begin to fail once they are pushed into continuous operation. This is why early warning signs tend to appear right when temperatures rise.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"402e0a25","settings":{"title":"1. Your AC Is Blowing Warm Air or Feels Less Effective\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2699f46b","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">One of the most noticeable warning signs is an air conditioner blowing warm air or struggling to maintain your desired temperature.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This often points to:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Low refrigerant or clear refrigerant leak signs<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Early stages of compressor failure<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A thermostat not responding properly<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"42d2fa03","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You may also notice humid indoor air, which indicates your system is no longer removing moisture effectively.<\/span><\/p><p><strong>\ud83d\udca1 <i>Technician insight:<\/i><\/strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> In many service calls, reduced cooling is one of the earliest indicators that deeper system issues are developing.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2b64a1a7","settings":{"title":"2. Weak Airflow or Rooms That Never Cool Down\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4c0a4686","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.magnoliaairllc.com\/troubleshooting-poor-airflow-from-ac-vents\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> airflow feels weak<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> or uneven, your system may be losing its ability to circulate air properly.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Common causes include:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A worn evaporator fan motor<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Blocked or dirty coils that need condenser coil cleaning<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A frozen evaporator coil restricting airflow<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"18a6a62d","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Weak airflow forces your system to work harder, accelerating wear and increasing the likelihood of failure.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"108721c4","settings":{"title":"3. Frequent Short Cycling and Rising Energy Bills\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3cc0b643","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If your system turns on and off frequently without completing a full cycle, you are dealing with frequent short cycling.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This can be caused by:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Electrical issues such as blowing fuse<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Failing components like capacitor failure<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Thermostat malfunctions<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"470dcb14","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At the same time, you may notice high electricity bills. When your system runs inefficiently, energy consumption increases without delivering better comfort.<\/span><\/p><p><strong>\ud83d\udca1 <i>Technician insight:<\/i><\/strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Short cycling is one of the fastest ways to wear out a system because it repeatedly starts under high load.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5cd15980","settings":{"title":"4. Loud Noises or Unusual Smells\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"303a8c9","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your AC should not draw attention to itself. If it does, something is wrong.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4949218d","settings":{"title":"Warning Sounds:\n","header_size":"h3","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Como-ExtraBold","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":30,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}],"__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"14d0a8b6","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.magnoliaairllc.com\/why-is-my-ac-making-strange-sounds\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">clanking sound in AC<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> may indicate loose or broken parts<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Grinding or buzzing often points to motor or electrical issues<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">AC making loud noises usually signals internal damage<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5edda087","settings":{"title":"Warning Smells:\n","header_size":"h3","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Como-ExtraBold","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":30,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}],"__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6a80e5e1","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Musty odors may indicate mold growth<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Strange AC smells can signal buildup inside the system<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">An electrical burning smell should be addressed immediately<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3258bd8f","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These symptoms often appear before a major breakdown.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5b46a9ec","settings":{"title":"5. Leaks, Ice, or an Aging System\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5c62d9ae","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Visible issues are often the clearest indicators that your system is nearing the end of its lifespan.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"447765ed","settings":{"title":"Water or Refrigerant Leaks\n","header_size":"h3","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Como-ExtraBold","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":30,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}],"__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"62a3b9d","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Water leaking around AC may indicate a clogged drain<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Refrigerant leaks reduce performance and damage components<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6e7f1b65","settings":{"title":"Ice Formation\n","header_size":"h3","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Como-ExtraBold","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":30,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}],"__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4ea16f99","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A frozen evaporator coil is often a sign of airflow or refrigerant issues.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"23777382","settings":{"title":"AC Unit Age\n","header_size":"h3","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Como-ExtraBold","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":30,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}],"__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"47d6306c","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If your system is over 10 to 15 years old, AC unit age becomes a major factor. Older systems, especially those using <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.epa.gov\/section608\/refrigerant-management-program\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">R-22 refrigerant<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, are more prone to breakdowns and costly repairs.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"114570ea","settings":{"title":"Repair or Replace? A Practical Way to Decide\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"53161e27","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When multiple issues appear, it is important to weigh your options.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The 5000 rule HVAC is a helpful guideline:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Multiply the repair cost by the system\u2019s age<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the result exceeds 5000, replacement is usually the better investment<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"30f8fdba","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Modern systems with improved SEER2 efficiency offer better performance and lower energy costs.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5d2dc374","settings":{"title":"What You Should Do If You Notice These Signs\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3fb304e","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If your AC is showing any of these warning signs, taking early action can prevent bigger problems.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Start with these steps:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Check and replace your air filter<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Make sure your thermostat is working properly<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Turn off the system if you notice overheating or burning smells<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Schedule an inspection with a qualified HVAC technician<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2152f5b9","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Waiting too long can turn a minor repair into a complete system failure.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3e41b7e1","settings":{"title":"How to Reduce the Risk of Breakdown\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3be4a4ef","settings":{"editor":"<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.energy.gov\/energysaver\/air-conditioning\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Preventative care<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> plays a major role in system longevity.<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Schedule an annual tune-up before peak season<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Stay consistent with HVAC maintenance<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Keep coils clean and airflow unobstructed<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Monitor performance changes over time<\/span><\/li><\/ul>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3df1e566","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These steps help reduce the likelihood of needing emergency AC service during extreme heat.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7d83fdf0","settings":{"title":"Frequently Asked Questions\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"331f8d31","settings":{"items":[{"item_title":"What is the earliest sign that an AC is failing?","_id":"c2e9d99"},{"item_title":"Can I run my AC if it is blowing warm air?","_id":"7c836e1"},{"item_title":"How do I know if my compressor is failing?","_id":"4ab776e"},{"_id":"9de27a0","item_title":"Is it worth repairing an older AC unit?"},{"_id":"820eaf4","item_title":"Is it worth repairing an older AC unit?"}],"title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Como-ExtraBold","title_typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":30,"sizes":[]},"title_typography_font_weight":"600","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"0b8c887"}],"__globals__":{"title_typography_typography":"","normal_icon_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary","normal_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent"}},"elements":[{"id":"12dd1236","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"3dc7371"}]},"elements":[{"id":"3eb2aa36","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Reduced cooling performance or weak airflow is often the first sign that something is wrong.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"62564546","settings":{"_title":"item #2","content_width":"full","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"46f785b"}]},"elements":[{"id":"54a42ae5","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It is best to turn it off and have it inspected. Running it can worsen damage, especially if refrigerant levels are low.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"3ce542b8","settings":{"_title":"item #3","content_width":"full","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"3eb298a"}]},"elements":[{"id":"7cac2b83","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Signs include loud noises, poor cooling, and system shutdowns. Compressor failure often leads to major repairs.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"3632565c","settings":{"_title":"Item #4","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"8e0cf9e"}]},"elements":[{"id":"71ed5183","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the system is older and requires frequent repairs, replacement may be more cost-effective.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"412f7662","settings":{"_title":"Item #5","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"241f802"}]},"elements":[{"id":"67ae47","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Regular maintenance, timely repairs, and proper airflow management can significantly extend system lifespan.<\/span><\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"f691f39"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true}],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"nested-accordion","elType":"widget"},{"id":"15f1f30","settings":{"title":"Have a Cool Home in this Summer Heat\n","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"e96465f"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"551bd36e","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Air conditioners rarely fail without warning. From weak airflow and frequent short cycling to unusual noises and rising energy bills, these issues signal that your system is under stress.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In Dry Prong\u2019s demanding summer climate, ignoring these warning signs can lead to a complete breakdown at the worst possible time. Recognizing the early signs your AC is dying gives you the opportunity to act before small problems become major ones.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If your AC is alr